mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course focuses on the interdisciplinary application of artificial intelligence (AI) in environmental health, systematically explaining the methodological principles and practical applications of AI technologies in environmental epidemiology, exposure assessment, mechanism exploration, risk early warning and other fields. Adopting the mode of "method explanation + case analysis + practical training", it compares the advantages and disadvantages of classical analytical methods and AI methods, and also introduces the application of large language models in this field and the construction of vertical models, aiming to cultivate students' ability to solve practical environmental health problems with AI, with both theoretical and practical characteristics.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
